From: OPIZ3 br2-external
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-zero3: add vdd-cpu ramp delay

The AXP313A DCDC2 regulator has no ramp delay in the driver or DT, so
cpufreq raises the CPU clock right after the voltage write while the
rail is still slewing. With cpufreq active this caused random oopses
(faults on non-memory instructions) and RCU stalls. Use the same
200 uV/us as the BigTreeTech CB1 (H616 + AXP313A).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
 				regulator-always-on;
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <810000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1100000>;
+				regulator-ramp-delay = <200>;
 				regulator-name = "vdd-cpu";
 			};
 
